# ── Route-aware fallback (replaces the old `/* /index.html 200` catch-all) ──
# Why: the catch-all made EVERY nonexistent URL on www.sirinx.co answer 200
# with the SPA shell (soft-404), so crawlers and uptime checks could not see
# real breakage and unknown paths became duplicate content. With no catch-all,
# unmatched paths reach 404.html and Cloudflare Pages serves it with a real
# 404 status. See docs/seo/TECHNICAL_SEO_FIX_PACK_20260926.md.
# Guarded by shared/staticDeploySurface.test.ts.

# The only client-rendered subtree left is the robots-disallowed admin area.
# /projects/:slug and /blog/:slug pages are prerendered (server/ogTags.ts
# getStaticSeoRoutes), so unknown slugs under them must hit the real 404.
/admin /index.html 200
/admin/* /index.html 200

# Everything else resolves as a static file (prerendered routes) or as an
# honest 404 via 404.html. Do not re-add a `/*` catch-all here.
